<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26751" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lippĭo</span></b> , īvi,
			ītum, 4, v. n.
		lippus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to haw watery</i> or <i>inflamed eyes,
				to be blear-eyed</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: cum leviter lippirem, has litteras
			dedi, * <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 7, 14, 1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne omnino lippiatur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					28, 8, 27, § 94</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calor adjuvat lippientes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 1,
					9</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 29, 6, 38, §
			128</span></i>.— * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lippiunt fauces fame,</span>”
				i. e. <i>burn</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Curc. 2, 3, 37</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
